{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Cross-reference: this story's RED PROOF cannot be replayed from the tree\n\nMeasured at `origin/main` `339c0b3af7b`; full evidence on `d278-3792` (`relates_to` this\nticket).\n\nThe RED PROOF criterion replays \"one of the 4 named seam-guard modules\" as a change. All\nguard modules added by the split commits the epic cites are **already deleted**:\n`test_fetch_paging_split.py`, `test_processors_status_split.py`,\n`test_prompt_model_module_seam.py`, `test_config_resolver_seam.py`,\n`test_init_ensures_seam.py`. The proof must therefore replay a diff from git history\n(e.g. `git show b91f8f6830c`), not a module present in the tree.\n\nTwo further corrections to this description's gap statement:\n\n- **\"88 held-out twins left behind ... because it had no merge step\"** — the convention was\n  retired outright (`0b5d004f394`), epic `6ed2-24e5` is closed, and 0 tracked files match\n  `heldout`/`held_out`. There is no twin-producing convention to cite as evidence.\n- **\"around 30 modules that re-ran lint scripts over the real tree\"** — the existing comment\n  already records that the rubric currently BLESSES this shape (guard (iii) plus the Rule-5\n  structural-artifact exception), so flagging it is a change in the rubric's judgement, not\n  a gap in its coverage.\n\nShape 3 (**LOC floor/ceiling pinning**) is the one shape with both an uncovered rubric gap\nand a standing ADR behind it: ADR 0058 decides \"No other test may assert an upper LOC bound\non a `src/rebar` file, and none may hard-code a ceiling value\", and nothing enforces it."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793695636454320001,"uuid":"2edda1be-b540-4de3-bf31-a1dd79efc2a8"}